// Title: Sysmon Discovery Via Default Driver Altitude Using Findstr.EXE
// Sigma ID: 37db85d1-b089-490a-a59a-c7b6f984f480
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: frack113
// Date: 2021-12-16 | Modified: 2023-11-14
// ATT&CK: discovery, T1518.001
// Description: Detects usage of "findstr" with the argument "385201". Which could indicate potential discovery
//   of an installed Sysinternals Sysmon service using the default driver altitude (even if the name
//   is changed).
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/f339e7da7d05f6057fdfcdd3742bfcf365fee2a9/atomics/T1518.001/T1518.001.md#atomic-test-5---security-software-discovery---sysmon-service
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_findstr_sysmon_discovery_via_default_altitude.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ((FolderPath endswith "\\find.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\findstr.exe") or (ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName in~ ("FIND.EXE", "FINDSTR.EXE"))) and ProcessCommandLine contains " 385201"
